From b3c50a2b3f9bf6b1f2b48673de8f235ace975c8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: two video streams of one picture, Dolby Vision
 and HDR10+, play as the setting chooses

Some files carry the same picture twice, as a video stream with Dolby
Vision of its own and one of HDR10+ without it. Nothing chose between
them: Kodi opened the first stream flagged default, or the first, so the
format that played depended on the order of the tracks, whatever "Videos
with both Dolby Vision and HDR10+" (videoscreen.hadesdualhdr) says and
whatever the display takes.

CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::ChooseHdrStream(), when the streams of a file are made,
finds such a pair (a stream with a Dolby Vision record, and one of HDR10
or HDR10+ without Dolby Vision; two tracks of one Dolby Vision picture are
one stream there) and asks DVBRIDGE::TwoStreamsOf(): on a display that
takes both, the setting chooses, as for one stream with both, HDR10+ only
where that stream has HDR10+ metadata; on a display that takes one of the
two, that one, its own Dolby Vision natively or its own HDR10+ metadata
rather than the other made into it; elsewhere the stream Kodi opens.
Whether the HDR10 stream has HDR10+ metadata is known from its first
packets, which are read ahead (FindHdr10Plus(), at most 24 of its access
units, 600 packets, 32 MiB or 1.5 s, as the read ahead for soft telecine
does) only where the choice depends on it and the file is read from its
start by a plain input; the packets go to the player afterwards, as if
they had not been read. VideoPlayer opens that stream unless the user
chose a video stream for the file. kodi.log says what the file has, what
the display takes, what was read and which stream plays. The help of the
setting says so, in English and in Spanish.

Found by SamuriHL in his CoreELEC builds (his preference there is a
setting of its own and does not read the packets).

Tests (outside the tree): five Matroska files made with mkvmerge 97 from
a Dolby Vision stream with its RPUs and an HDR10+ stream whose SEI was
made with FFmpeg's own serializer (FFmpeg 9.0.2's decoder finds its
SMPTE ST 2094-40 metadata; none in the HDR10 stream without it): the two
in either order, an HDR10 stream without HDR10+ and a Dolby Vision one,
one Dolby Vision stream, two HDR10+ streams; opened with FFmpeg 9.0.2 and
run through the real ChooseHdrStream(), FindHdr10Plus(),
DetermineHdrType(), DVPlaybackPolicy.h and CDVHdr10Plus::Read(), for
seven cases of the setting and the display: 35 checks, among them that
the packets read ahead are the first of the file in their order and that
nothing is read where the choice does not need it. Before the change 21
of them fail. 10 mutants, each seen. Text checks of the help.
